<!-- Pacific Strike CIA memorandum event, adapted from Strike Group Molniya U.S.-voice interstitial format. -->
<Page
  xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
  xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
  xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
  xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
  mc:Ignorable="d"
  d:DesignWidth="1920"
  d:DesignHeight="1080">
  <Viewbox>
    <Border Background="White" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" Width="864" Height="1120" Padding="45"
            TextElement.FontFamily="Courier New" TextElement.Foreground="Black" TextElement.FontSize="16">
      <Border.Effect>
        <DropShadowEffect />
      </Border.Effect>

      <Border BorderThickness="0,10,10,10" BorderBrush="#FF000000">
        <Grid>
          <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
            <RowDefinition Height="10"/>
            <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
          </Grid.RowDefinitions>
          <TextBlock Text="C05084534" Background="#FFFFFFFF" HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Top" Margin="17,-15,0,0" Padding="5,0,5,0" />
          <Grid Grid.Row="0">
            <Grid.RowDefinitions>
              <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
              <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
              <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
              <RowDefinition Height="10"/>
              <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
              <RowDefinition Height="15"/>
              <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
              <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
              <RowDefinition Height="15"/>
              <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
            </Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
              <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
              <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
              <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
              <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="4" Text="TOP SECRET" TextAlignment="Center"/>
            <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="4" Grid.RowSpan="2" TextAlignment="Center" FontFamily="Times New Roman">
              Main Intelligence Directorate
              <LineBreak/>
              <LineBreak/>
              <Run FontSize="12">Moscow, 62665</Run>
            </TextBlock>
            <TextBlock Grid.Row="4" Grid.Column="3" Text="17 February 1988"/>
            <TextBlock Grid.Row="6" Grid.Column="3" Text="222X1"/>
            <TextBlock Grid.Row="7" Grid.Column="0" Text="MEMORANDUM FOR:   "/>
            <TextBlock Grid.Row="7" Grid.Column="1" TextWrapping="Wrap">
              VMF HIGH COMMAND
              <LineBreak/>
              RED BANNER PACIFIC FLEET
              <LineBreak/>
              10th SUBMARINE DIV//J2//
              <LineBreak/>
              11th SUBMARINE DIV//J2//			  
            </TextBlock>
            <TextBlock Grid.Row="7" Grid.Column="3" TextWrapping="Wrap">
              EO 13526 3.3(b)(1)&gt;25Yrs
              <LineBreak/>
              EO 13526 3.5(c)
            </TextBlock>
            <TextBlock Grid.Row="9" Grid.Column="0" Text="SUBJECT:   "/>
            <TextBlock Grid.Row="9" Grid.Column="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="3" Text="USN comms traffic from NIMITZ CVBG command net"/>
          </Grid>
          <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" TextWrapping="Wrap">
            1. SIGINT station VARYAG has passed American command comms regarding destruction of NIMITZ supply convoy. Traffic reflects urgent concern for rearm and refuel of NIMITZ CVBG and likelihood that Western Pacific Area will be left with organic land-based airpower only.  
            <LineBreak/>
            <LineBreak/>
            2. USN command channels direct NIMITZ CVBG to make best speed for Pearl Harbor in light of Soviet surface and submerged presence interdicting supply between Hawaii and Iwo Jima. NIMITZ's orders include demand for transit made at best speed, disregarding counter-sub zig-zagging, with  optimistic comments regarding USN carrier ASW aircraft's ability to screen CVBGs from friendly submarines. 
            <LineBreak/>
            <LineBreak/>
            3. Expect NIMITZ CVBG to concentrate limited avgas reserves on ASW flights, reducing ASuW and CAP sortie generation. 
            <LineBreak/>
            <LineBreak/>
			4. American commanders understand that their limited land-based and carrier-based airpower is insufficient to stop friendly encirclement of Tokyo or complete friendly occupation of Japan. With 2 functional CVGBs remaining in Pacific Theater, the GRU assesses that destruction of any CVBG will result in collapse of enemy resistance in Japan, and likely start of peace talks between the USSR and America. 
            <LineBreak/>
            <LineBreak/>
          </TextBlock>
          <TextBlock TextAlignment="Right" Text="Vladlen Mikhailov, Director" HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Top" Margin="480,500,0,0" Grid.Row="2"/>
          <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Grid.RowSpan="3" VerticalAlignment="Bottom">
            <Run TextDecorations="Underline">Distribution by ER/01 March 1988 w/Atts</Run>
            <LineBreak/>
            <LineBreak/>
            Orig - Each Addressee
            <LineBreak/>
               1 - 2nd Directorate GRU
            <LineBreak/>
               1 - 6th Directorate GRU
            <LineBreak/>
               1 - 12th Directorate GRU
          </TextBlock>
          <TextBlock Grid.Row="4" Text="TOP SECRET" TextAlignment="Center"/>
        </Grid>
      </Border>
    </Border>
  </Viewbox>
</Page>
